WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.159
Infiltrator

00:00:02.159 --> 00:00:05.920
phrase,

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:10.240
don't make a move.

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.480
Single move.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.240
I'm going to blow the circuits out of

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.750
that synthetic skull of yours.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:19.920
[Music]

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.320
You're human, huh?

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.880
That's what they all say. I'll be the

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:26.960
judge of that.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.960
Hold still. I'm going to examine you.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.320
Check you for serial numbers.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.920
What did I say? Don't move.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.559
[Music]

00:00:40.559 --> 00:00:47.600
Okay.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.559
Look up

00:00:50.559 --> 00:00:57.300
to the left.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.160
[Laughter]

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:03.039
Lift your arms. Higher.

00:01:03.039 --> 00:01:15.680
Higher.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.439
Looks pretty human to me.

00:01:19.439 --> 00:01:27.520
Flesh and blood.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.960
So, you really are a human.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:33.840
I'm just going to pet you in real quick.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:38.640
Don't move. Checking you for weapons.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.740
Okay.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:48.640
[Music]

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:51.840
Okay. You're all clear.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.560
So, you really are a human.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.159
Would have been a shame if I had to take

00:01:56.159 --> 00:02:01.840
out such a cute looking model.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:04.719
So, you're wild, a civilian.

00:02:04.719 --> 00:02:06.000
What are you doing out here in the

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.959
wasteland?

00:02:08.959 --> 00:02:18.959
You are in bad shape.

00:02:18.959 --> 00:02:22.319
Yeah. Sorry about the little mishap. You

00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:25.440
know how dangerous those infiltrators

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.040
are. Yeah,

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.560
but it looks like you are just some

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.360
random civilian

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:39.200
and whatever you were up to, you are not

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:43.519
in good condition at all.

00:02:43.519 --> 00:02:50.560
You're bleeding a lot.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:55.840
Do you know what day it is?

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:58.640
Okay.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:11.440
Can you follow my fingers?

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:15.440
you're not looking so hot and that's not

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:19.120
part of my mission. I'm not meant to do

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:22.720
rescue or whatever.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.640
My superior is going to be pissed at me,

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:31.710
but I can't leave you like this.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:34.480
[Music]

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.360
This is Zarya Kennedy. Uh, found a

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.760
survivor out here. Going to need a

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.400
rescue chopper.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:46.799
>> Yeah, send it to my coordinates.

00:03:46.799 --> 00:03:50.799
>> Yeah, you can just call me easy. Don't

00:03:50.799 --> 00:03:53.599
worry about the formalities. Uh, you

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:56.560
look a little dehydrated

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:58.560
here. I have some water. I've got some

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:16.799
here.

00:04:16.799 --> 00:04:19.199
Well, you don't trust me.

00:04:19.199 --> 00:04:32.160
Here, I'll show you. It's fine.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.240
Delicious.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:37.600
It might have a little dust in it. Here,

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:41.280
take a drink.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:47.440
Yeah, just drink as much as you can.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:53.520
Good.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:56.960
Yeah, I am not usually out doing stuff

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:02.320
like this. My mission is just to

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:05.680
do recon and locate the Skynet superco

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.360
computer.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.440
My resistance group is planning a pretty

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:13.120
big attack, but you have nothing to do

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.320
with that and you're just kind of caught

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:18.880
in this mess. So,

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:21.600
I don't feel right just letting you die

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:28.400
out here.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:32.080
I'm going to do some first aid.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.720
Just enough to keep you from killing

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:56.639
over until the rescue team gets here.

00:05:56.639 --> 00:06:02.160
Going to have to patch you up a bit, but

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:12.240
it's not going to feel very good.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:13.840
All right. So, I'm just going to clean

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:17.120
your wounds a bit.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:21.840
We've got alcohol swabs here.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:23.360
It's going to sting like hell. You know

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.440
the drill.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:28.000
Don't scream. We can't be drawing any

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:35.280
more attention to this area.

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:52.319
Okay, you're taking it pretty good.

00:06:52.319 --> 00:06:55.360
Yeah, you've got a good amount of damage

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:59.919
to your face. And I see that there's

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:02.880
something even worse here on your arm.

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:09.520
This one's going to need stitches.

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:11.360
Okay,

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:13.440
that's clean enough.

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:14.880
I have to close the wood or you're going

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:18.960
to bleed out.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:23.840
Yeah. Just uh look away.

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:25.840
Think happy thoughts or something like

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:32.880
that.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:36.080
Yeah, I know. I don't have anesthetic.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:44.000
Sorry.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:47.919
Just doing a quick little stitch up.

00:07:47.919 --> 00:07:50.479
Yeah, I know it hurts. You're going to

00:07:50.479 --> 00:07:53.039
be all right.

00:07:53.039 --> 00:08:12.800
Just try not to make too much noise.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:22.000
Okay,

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:26.000
that should be good. I'm just going to

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:32.159
cut that.

00:08:32.159 --> 00:08:54.000
Okay.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:56.000
All right, I'm going to wrap your arm

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:58.880
and just

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:08.959
close that up.

00:09:08.959 --> 00:09:27.760
Okay.

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:31.440
I know this is a sloppy job. This is

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:34.640
Not my forte.

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:37.040
I

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:39.760
don't usually find any civilians out

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:44.000
here at all.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:46.000
Okay, looks like that should be good

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:58.240
enough.

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:13.680
Okay, just let me finish this wrapping.

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:16.800
Yeah, that should be

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:25.440
good there.

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:27.839
Okay, so

00:10:27.839 --> 00:10:30.000
the bleeding is somewhat under control,

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.600
but

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:41.120
probably going to need more gauze.

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:44.160
I'm just going to bandage you up.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:46.560
You've got

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:49.279
just going to bandage that

00:10:49.279 --> 00:10:51.839
spot on your forehead

00:10:51.839 --> 00:10:53.920
so you don't bleed into your eyes or

00:10:53.920 --> 00:11:08.079
something.

00:11:08.079 --> 00:11:16.480
Right about there.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:24.560
Okay.

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:27.519
I know you're in a lot of pain,

00:11:27.519 --> 00:11:29.200
but I'm going to need you to suck it up.

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:31.680
Okay. There's another one right here.

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:39.200
I'm just going to clean up.

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:40.880
Oh, what do you want to know about me?

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:42.640
my life.

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:46.399
Well, I'm just a resistance soldier.

00:11:46.399 --> 00:11:50.160
I do what I have to do.

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:56.399
Not much more to it than that.

00:11:56.399 --> 00:12:06.720
What you you mean before judgment day?

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:08.639
You know,

00:12:08.639 --> 00:12:10.240
the world is a completely different

00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:14.800
place now.

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:20.240
Whatever life I had back then is gone.

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:29.120
Whatever person I was back then is dead.

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:31.200
So,

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:55.279
there's no sense dwelling on the past.

00:12:55.279 --> 00:12:57.839
If you ask me, as far as I'm concerned,

00:12:57.839 --> 00:13:02.800
it didn't happen.

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:04.800
Feels like

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:13.360
a lifetime ago.

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:17.600
But enough about me.

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:22.320
What is someone like you doing here?

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:29.440
What's your name?

00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:31.360
Well, then

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:38.320
none of that matters now, does it?

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:48.320
right here.

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:50.959
But if that's what you were,

00:13:50.959 --> 00:13:54.079
then what in the world has brought you

00:13:54.079 --> 00:13:56.000
out here?

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:58.800
You look like hell, to be honest. You do

00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:05.680
not look like a regular civilian.

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:09.040
The research facility.

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:11.920
You mean that Skynet one that uses human

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:15.120
test subjects and experiments on them,

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:20.800
tortures them? You were there.

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:23.600
You escaped.

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:25.920
How in the world did you get out of

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:31.440
there?

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:35.519
Well, you're here now.

00:14:35.519 --> 00:14:37.680
So, when I was searching you, I found

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:40.800
some things on you. Not quite weapons,

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:46.399
but

00:14:46.399 --> 00:14:51.040
the hell is this crap?

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:54.399
You just escaped barely with your life

00:14:54.399 --> 00:14:58.000
and you have

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:10.560
these random pieces of junk.

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:12.399
Toys

00:15:12.399 --> 00:15:15.279
for a friend.

00:15:15.279 --> 00:15:16.959
A friend who like to collect this kind

00:15:16.959 --> 00:15:21.120
of stuff.

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:27.680
Huh?

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:30.160
You think I look like them?

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:32.000
No, I'm

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:35.440
I'm not related to anyone like that. I

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:40.800
don't think I'm related to anyone.

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:43.279
But seems like you care a lot about

00:15:43.279 --> 00:15:44.880
them.

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:48.000
So, you've just been

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:53.600
going searching through the wasteland,

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:55.519
hoping you'll be reunited with this

00:15:55.519 --> 00:16:00.959
friend of yours,

00:16:00.959 --> 00:16:03.759
collecting these little things you find,

00:16:03.759 --> 00:16:09.040
risking your life for them.

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:13.360
It's kind of stupid, but

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:15.440
no, like

00:16:15.440 --> 00:16:19.680
I get it.

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:23.279
You have a lot of physical damage

00:16:23.279 --> 00:16:27.839
and so I know you're in a lot of pain,

00:16:27.839 --> 00:16:32.639
but when I look in your eyes, I can tell

00:16:32.639 --> 00:16:38.959
it's more than just physical, isn't it?

00:16:38.959 --> 00:16:40.639
You don't know if you'll ever see them

00:16:40.639 --> 00:16:44.399
again.

00:16:44.399 --> 00:16:47.120
And you just keep hanging on to

00:16:47.120 --> 00:16:50.800
something that will

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:55.519
let you have a little bit of hope.

00:16:55.519 --> 00:16:59.279
I can understand that.

00:16:59.279 --> 00:17:07.120
It's pretty brave if you ask me.

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:11.199
All this time

00:17:11.199 --> 00:17:15.439
you've spent fighting for survival.

00:17:15.439 --> 00:17:17.679
I'm sure your friend has been doing the

00:17:17.679 --> 00:17:21.360
same. Just don't let go of that bright

00:17:21.360 --> 00:17:23.760
hope you have.

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:27.360
I let go of mine a long time ago.

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:30.400
But I admire you for that.

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:33.360
For

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:38.640
not letting anything get in your way.

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:41.280
You've gotten this far. You've been

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:50.799
through so much.

00:17:50.799 --> 00:17:56.400
No matter what else comes to get you,

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:58.960
you're going to be

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:02.000
strong. I can tell.

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:10.320
You're not going down without a fight.

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:14.320
So, take this back.

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:16.400
Take all of them. I'm not going to

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:19.280
confiscate them.

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:21.280
You need them for whenever you find that

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:23.360
person.

00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:25.760
I think you will.

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:32.080
Just keep looking and don't give up.

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:38.000
Keep hanging on.

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:40.799
Looks like the rescue chopper is here.

00:18:40.799 --> 00:18:42.240
They're going to take you back to our

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:43.919
base

00:18:43.919 --> 00:18:46.880
and you'll be safe from there. They'll

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:48.960
help you find your way. It was nice to

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:53.440
meet you.

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:55.600
Maybe I'll catch you around sometime

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:59.120
half dead in the wasteland once again.

00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:04.960
Next time I might not be so merciful.

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:09.679
No, we have a common enemy and

00:19:09.679 --> 00:19:12.799
I trust that you are on my side.

00:19:12.799 --> 00:19:16.720
So if you ever need help from me and you

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:20.400
see me around, I'll have your back.

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:22.880
I'll remember your face.

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:26.880
I don't forget people once I meet them.

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:30.080
The rescue team is here for you.

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:32.480
They'll make sure you're okay. So, get

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:35.280
going.

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:38.640
You've got a lot of healing to do.

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:43.640
See you around.
